{
  "summary": "This study investigates how dual twisted interfaces in CVD-grown trilayer MoS2 affect second harmonic generation (SHG). By fabricating nine distinct stacking configurations, researchers measured Raman and photoluminescence responses to identify stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic behaviors. Atomic-resolution microscopy confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice. The study developed a framework predicting SHG intensity and polarization based on interface geometry, demonstrating TT-MoS2's potential for tunable nonlinear optical engineering.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CVD-grown trilayer MoS2 with dual twisted interfaces exhibits stacking-dependent phonon and excitonic responses",
    "Atomic-resolution techniques confirmed dual twisted interfaces and a supermoiré lattice structure",
    "A framework linking interface geometry to SHG intensity and polarization was established"
  ],
  "study_type": "CVD-grown twisted trilayer MoS2 configurations",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a foundational understanding of multi-interface twisted stacking effects on nonlinear optical responses in 2D materials, enabling precise engineering of second harmonic generation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses residual tumor persistence after high-frequency irreversible electroporation (H-FIRE) for prostate cancer. By identifying DNA damage repair as the key mechanism for reversible cell survival, researchers engineered piezoelectric nanomaterial BOIS. H-FIRE-induced membrane permeabilization enables BOIS delivery to residual cells. Ultrasound activation triggers BOIS to generate electric fields and reactive oxygen species, causing irreversible cell death through dual mechanisms. This approach significantly enhances tumor eradication by converting reversible injury to irreversible damage.",
  "key_findings": [
    "H-FIRE-induced membrane permeabilization facilitates BOIS delivery to residual prostate cancer cells",
    "Ultrasound-activated BOIS generates electric fields and reactive oxygen species to induce irreversible cell death",
    "The dual mechanism converts reversible tumor injury to irreversible lethal damage, enhancing eradication"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a self-reinforcing therapeutic loop where focal ablation delivers nanomaterials to eliminate residual disease, offering a novel strategy for complete tumor eradication post-focal therapy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how the blood-brain barrier (BBB) selectively transports neuroprotective proteins into the brain. Using bioorthogonal proteomics, researchers identified 191 plasma proteins sampled and 92 transported across the healthy BBB. These proteins, enriched for carrier and metabolic functions, target specific brain cells like astrocytes and microglia via receptor-mediated mechanisms involving APOA1 and ABCA1. Early Alzheimer's disease models show altered transport, with reduced APOA1 and increased SERPINA1 uptake, while hepatic APOA1 overexpression rescues synaptic and behavioral deficits in these models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The healthy BBB samples 191 plasma proteins and permits 92 into the brain parenchyma.",
    "APOA1 crosses the BBB via SR-B1 and engages astrocytic ABCA1, a key Alzheimer's risk gene, driving cholesterol efflux for synapse integrity.",
    "Early-stage 5xFAD Alzheimer's models exhibit reduced APOA1 and increased SERPINA1 uptake, reversible by hepatic APOA1 overexpression."
  ],
  "study_type": "Bioorthogonal proteomics",
  "scientific_significance": "This work redefines the BBB as a selective interface that recruits neuroprotective circulatory proteins to maintain brain health, highlighting critical pathways for neuroprotection in early Alzheimer's disease."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates restoring functional responses in aged CD8+ T cells using miRNA delivery via PEI-functionalized silicon nanowires. The approach involves transient modulation of transcriptional programs to enhance activation, proliferation, and differentiation. Results show single miRNA delivery improves early activation, while multiplexed delivery boosts effector functions, metabolic health, and sustained effector priming in aged human and murine cells.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Single miRNA delivery enhances early T cell activation and differentiation in aged populations",
    "Multiplexed miRNA delivery significantly improves effector functions, metabolic health, and proliferation in aged CD8+ T cells",
    "The nanowire platform maintains functional efficacy across diverse aged human donors, including cancer patients"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro and in vivo delivery platform",
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a targeted strategy to reverse age-related T cell dysfunction through precise miRNA modulation, offering a potential pathway for enhancing immune responses in aging populations."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines human brain cellular xenograft (HBCX) models as in vivo platforms for studying human brain physiology and pathology. The models transplant human pluripotent stem cell-derived cells into immunodeficient mice, revealing human-specific phenotypes, disease mechanisms, and enabling functional genomics, drug testing, and biomarker discovery. They address species differences in neuroimmunology, particularly microglia-related pathways.",
  "key_findings": [
    "HBCXs enable in vivo study of human brain-specific cellular and molecular phenotypes",
    "These models reveal human disease mechanisms inaccessible in traditional systems",
    "HBC: models provide a scalable platform for functional genomics and drug testing"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "HBCX models advance neuroimmunology by providing an in vivo system to study human-specific cellular interactions and disease mechanisms, overcoming limitations of in vitro and animal models."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the challenge of observing distributed cortical circuits during natural behavior using a novel 1-gram wireless mesoscope called Airscope. It achieves 4 μm lateral resolution over a 6 mm field of view at 12.5 Hz, enabling high-throughput calcium imaging of up to 8,500 neurons per animal without tethering. The technology supports multi-animal recordings across diverse behavioral paradigms and reveals cortical activity patterns linked to social dominance, competition outcomes, and reward location during maze exploration.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Airscope enables wireless, high-resolution cortical imaging of up to 8,500 neurons per animal without tethering",
    "Cortical activity patterns correlate with social dominance and competition outcomes between animals",
    "Reward-location-associated cortical activity patterns are observed during maze exploration"
  ],
  "study_type": "Wireless mesoscope",
  "scientific_significance": "This technology bridges large-scale cortical recording with unconstrained natural behavior, advancing systems neuroscience by enabling multi-animal, high-resolution imaging across complex behavioral contexts."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed a microfluidic-based GradientScreen assay to evaluate ratiometric drug combinations in high-risk paediatric acute lymphob. The approach generated overlapping drug gradients and correlated response metrics with minimal residual disease and clinical outcomes. The system shows potential for identifying treatment-resistant cases and guiding alternative therapies in standard ALL protocols.",
  "key_findings": [
    "GradientScreen correlates combination response metrics with minimal residual disease post-treatment",
    "The assay predicts clinical outcomes using standard paediatric ALL treatment protocols",
    "It enables screening for alternative therapies in treatment-resistant cases"
  ],
  "study_type": "Microfluidic combination drug screening assay",
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a clinically translatable framework for precision oncology in paediatric leukaemia by linking functional drug response metrics to molecular markers and clinical outcomes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study developed DynaVelo, a generative neural ordinary differential equation model to predict single-cell multiomic dynamics in B cells. The model integrates gene expression and transcription factor activity from multiome data, enabling in silico perturbation to simulate loss-of-function and rescue effects. It identified Ctcf, Stat3, and Bcl6 as rescue targets for Arid1a heterozygous deficiency, validated by in vivo experiments in double-heterozygous mice.",
  "key_findings": [
    "DynaVelo predicts cell-state-specific gene regulatory networks disrupted in Arid1a heterozygous B cells",
    "In silico perturbation of Arid1aHet GCs identified Ctcf, Stat3, and Bcl6 as rescue targets",
    "In vivo validation confirmed rescue of dark-zone phenotypes in Arid1aHet;CtcfHet mice"
  ],
  "study_type": "Generative neural ordinary differential equation model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a framework for predicting functional perturbation effects in single-cell multiomic dynamics, advancing computational modeling of immune cell differentiation and disease mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how spatial confinement in germinal centers (GCs) influences B cell clonal diversity and immunodominance. Using mice with impaired GC confinement due to Gα13 deficiency, researchers observed reduced clonal diversification and increased clonal crossover between GCs. De-confined GCs exhibited decreased repertoire diversity and stronger immunodominance toward accessible epitopes, indicating confinement's role in maintaining antibody breadth through restricted clone spread.",
  "key_findings": [
    "De-confined GCs showed minimal clonal diversification compared to confined GCs",
    "Increased clonal crossover between neighboring GCs in confinement-defective lymph nodes",
    "De-confined GCs exhibited reduced repertoire diversity with heightened immunodominance toward accessible epitopes"
  ],
  "study_type": "Mouse models with Gα13 deficiency",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that spatial confinement in germinal centers moderates immunodominance and preserves antibody breadth by limiting dominant clone spread, providing mechanistic insight into how B cell responses achieve diverse antibody responses."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the microscopic origin of ionic memory in two-dimensional nanochannels using operando interferometric imaging and electrokinetic measurements. It directly visualizes voltage-induced blistering of confining walls as the cause of memristive hysteresis, identifying unidirectional blisters from electrostatic forces and bidirectional blusing from osmotic pressure. The findings provide a mechanistic framework for device behavior and variability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Direct visualization of voltage-induced blistering in 2D nanochannels as the origin of memristive hysteresis",
    "Identification of unidirectional blisters driven by electrostatic forces on surface charges",
    "Bidirectional blisters resulting from osmotic pressure due to concentration polarization"
  ],
  "study_type": "Operando interferometric imaging with electrokinetic measurements",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes electromechanical coupling as a direct mechanism for ionic memory in 2D nanochannels, advancing understanding of nanofluidic memristors and enabling more precise design of ionic-based computing systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the Late Holocene reexpansion of the Laurentide Ice Sheet (LIS) using ice core and geological evidence. It demonstrates that the LIS reexpanded ~2000 years ago after a minimum configuration established ~3.6 thousand years ago, marking the start of the next glaciation. The ice sheet reached maximum extent by ~1960 CE, subsequently retreating due to anthropogenic warming, ending the glaciation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The LIS achieved its minimum interglial dimensions ~3.6 thousand years ago",
    "Reexpansion occurred ~2000 years ago, initiating the next glaciation",
    "Maximum LIS extent reached ~1960 CE before anthropogenic-driven retreat"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings highlight how anthropogenic climate change can terminate glacial cycles by accelerating ice sheet retreat, providing evidence for greenhouse gas forcing's role in overriding natural climate cycles."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how group 2 innate lymphoid cells (ILC2s) influence tumor immunity via interleukin-9 (IL-9). Using human genomic data and mouse models, researchers found ILC2-derived IL-9 enhances eosinophil survival, retention, and cytotoxicity within tumors, promoting antitumor activity independent of adaptive immunity. Eosinophil depletion reversed tumor control, while eosinophil transfer restored it. The pathway was linked to improved outcomes in melanoma and lung cancer.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ILC2-derived IL-9 increases eosinophil survival and cytotoxicity in tumors",
    "Eosinophil ablation abolished GITR-mediated tumor control",
    "IL-9 and eosinophil signatures correlate with favorable prognosis in melanoma and lung adenocarcinoma"
  ],
  "study_type": "Genetic ablation mouse models and adoptive transfer experiments",
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies an innate immune pathway where ILC2s drive eosinophil-mediated tumor suppression, providing a mechanistic basis for targeting GITR to enhance antitumor immunity without adaptive lymphocyte involvement."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the material redirects expansion stress inward, suppresses electrode swelling, and enhances Li+ kinetics. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, with reduced expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect lithiation-induced stress inward, suppressing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composites achieve 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency",
    "The design reduces electrode expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles and enables 2 Ah NCM811 pouch cells with 80% capacity retention after 1200 cycles"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vitro engineering of silicon-carbon composites with heteroatom-doped carbon hosts",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable strategy for developing practical silicon-carbon anodes with minimal expansion and enhanced cycling stability in lithium-ion batteries."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated inter-individual variation in human striatum using single-nucleus RNA sequencing across 3.9 million nuclei from 178 donors. It found common patterns of astrocyte, microglia, and oligodendrocyte precursor cell abundance across gray matter regions. Age-related gene expression changes varied by cell type, with donor age predictable from RNA patterns (median error 6.6 years). Genetic variants influenced nearly 10,000 genes, predominantly cell-type specific and distinguishing striatal from cortical neurons.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Common astrocyte, microglia, and oligodendrocyte precursor cell abundance patterns across gray matter regions",
    "Age-associated gene expression changes differed by cell type, with donor age predictable from RNA patterns (median error 6.6 years)",
    "Genetic variants associated with nearly 10,000 genes, mostly cell-type specific and distinguishing striatal from cortical neurons"
  ],
  "study_type": "single-nucleus RNA sequencing",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a foundational resource for understanding human brain cellular and genetic variation, enabling future research on brain vulnerabilities and inter-individual differences."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how matrix viscoelasticity influences γδ T-cell phenotype and function. Using tunable collagen gels, researchers found slow-relaxing matrices preserved less differentiated states, reduced migration, and increased FAS/PD-1 expression while maintaining TNF-α and IFN-γ production. These cells also demonstrated improved tumor control in HCT116 models, highlighting viscoelastic cues as critical regulators of γδ T-cell differentiation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Slow-relaxing matrices preserved less differentiated γδ T-cell phenotypes",
    "Increased FAS and PD-1 expression with reduced migration",
    "Enhanced tumor control in HCT116 models despite elevated PD-1"
  ],
  "study_type": "Tunable collagen gel system",
  "scientific_significance": "The findings establish matrix viscoelasticity as a key regulator of post-thymic γδ T-cell differentiation and function, revealing mechanical cues as critical factors in immune cell behavior."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated SusC-reactive Th17 subsets in inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) patients using single-cell profiling. Researchers identified a TMIGD2hi Th1.7 subset spatially enriched at the intestinal epithelium, characterized by BACH2lo and GZMAhi. The subset expands in IBD, indicating a microbiome-reactive mechanism linked to loss of tolerance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A TMIGD2hi Th17 subset is spatially enriched at the intestinal epithelium",
    "The subset is BACH2lo and GZMAhi",
    "The subset expands in inflammatory bowel disease"
  ],
  "study_type": "single-cell profiling",
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a microbiome-reactive Th17 subset that provides mechanistic insight into how commensal-specific T cell responses contribute to mucosal inflammation in IBD."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the functional architecture of the human insula using intracranial electrical stimulation and electroencephalography in 87 participants. It identifies four distinct regions: a dorsal-posterior region processing nociceptive/thermoceptive signals, a ventral-posterior region integrating somatic information, a mid-anterior region linked to visceral sensations and anxiety, and an anterior-polar region involved in salience detection. The anterior region shows strong connections with the prefrontal cortex, enabling cognitive modulation of pain and bodily perception.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The insula has four distinct functional regions: dorsal-posterior for nociceptive/thermoceptive signals, ventral-posterior for somatic integration, mid-anterior for visceral sensations and anxiety, and anterior-polar for salience detection.",
    "The anterior-polar region exhibits strong prefrontal connections and influences other insular regions, enabling cognitive modulation of pain and bodily perception.",
    "This architecture links cytoarchitecture to asymmetric electrophysiological interactions, providing mechanistic insights into cognitive modulation of interoception."
  ],
  "study_type": "Intracranial electrical stimulation and electroencephalography",
  "scientific_significance": "This work defines a functional architecture of the human insula that connects cytoarchitecture to directed electrophysiological interactions, advancing understanding of how cognition modulates pain and bodily perception."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates biomimetic polyzwitterionic coacervates (pZCOs) for osteoarthritis treatment by replicating natural cartilage lubrication. The approach involves intra-articular delivery of pZCOs loaded with anti-inflammatory drugs and mesenchymal stem cells. Results show reduced cartilage degradation, suppressed inflammation, and improved joint function in animal models, outperforming clinical hyaluronic acid lubricants in lubrication, retention, and therapeutic efficacy.",
  "key_findings": [
    "pZCOs replicate natural cartilage lubrication with ultralow friction",
    "Intra-articular pZCOs reduce cartilage degradation and inflammation in osteoarthritis models",
    "pZCOs outperform clinical hyaluronic acid lubricants in lubrication performance and therapeutic efficacy"
  ],
  "study_type": "In vivo animal models",
  "scientific_significance": "Engineered biomimetic coacervates represent a novel strategy for integrated osteoarthritis management through dual lubrication and therapeutic payload delivery."
}

{
  "summary": "This study introduces recordanelles, a single-component synthetic organelle for transcriptome-wide single-cell RNA recording in human cells. The technology uses a mitochondrial membrane anchor, condensate assembler, and poly(A)-binding protein to capture and protect mRNAs over days. It preserves transient transcriptional responses from inducible promoters or interferon signaling at the single-cell level, enabling long-term unbiased transcriptome tracking without disrupting cellular processes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Recordanelles capture up to 90% of endogenous mRNAs in human cells",
    "The system preserves transient transcriptional responses from induc. promoters or interferon signaling over days",
    "Recordanelles enable nondisruptive, transcriptome-wide single-cell RNA recording without bias"
  ],
  "study_type": "Synthetic organelle",
  "scientific_significance": "This technology provides a method for long-term, unbiased transcriptome tracking at the single-cell level, advancing the ability to study dynamic biological processes without disrupting cellular function."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated transcriptome data from 1 million human neutrophils across 781 samples to create a single-cell atlas (SCAHN). It identified tissue-specific neutrophil subsets with distinct functions and gene expression changes in infections, cancer, immune suppression, and sex differences. The atlas also revealed neutrophil signatures predicting mortality in acute illness, cancer outcomes, and metabolic dysfunction.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of multiple tissue-specific neutrophil subsets with distinct functions",
    "Robust gene expression changes in neutrophils during infection, cancer, immune suppression, and sex differences",
    "Neutrophil-specific signatures predicting mortality in acute illness, cancer diagnosis, and metabolic dysfunction"
  ],
  "study_type": "Single-cell transcriptomic atlas",
  "scientific_significance": "This atlas provides a comprehensive reference for neutrophil heterogeneity across health and disease, enabling improved risk stratification and therapeutic targeting in immune-related conditions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates III-nitride-based in-sensor computing by leveraging interfacial polarization effects to overcome response loss and fabrication challenges in oxide or 2D-ferroelectric systems. The device achieves nanowatt-level sensitivity, 10^6 A/W responsivity, and 10^5 on/off ratios in sensor-memristor mode, with high-temperature stability up to 300°C. These properties enable efficient real-time intelligent analysis with minimal energy consumption.",
  "key_findings": [
    "III-nitride heterostructures exhibit defect-free bipolar polarization interfaces that prevent carrier recombination",
    "The device achieves nanowatt-level sensitivity and 10^6 A/W responsivity in sensor-memristor mode",
    "High-temperature stability up to 300°C supports industrial-scale manufacturing and integration"
  ],
  "study_type": "Device development",
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a design principle for interfacial-electrostatics-induced photocarrier separation and asymmetric-barriers-modulated transport, enabling energy-efficient in-sensor computing with robust thermal stability."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated a legal dispute involving David Sabatini, a biologist who won a $6 million defamation lawsuit against an accuser alleging sexual harassment and retaliation. The jury ruled in favor of Sabatini, dismissing the claims of misconduct. The outcome highlights the legal resolution of a high-profile case without confirming the alleged harassment or retaliation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A jury found David Sabatini liable for defamation claims",
    "The accuser's allegations of sexual harassment and retaliation were dismissed",
    "The lawsuit resulted in a $6 million financial award"
  ],
  "study_type": "",
  "scientific_significance": "This legal outcome provides insight into the resolution of high-profile harassment claims within scientific institutions but does not contribute directly to scientific understanding."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether immune cells directly transduce mechanical cues into nociceptive signals during ulcerative colitis. Using a minimally inflammatory zymosan model, researchers identified Piezo1 in CX3CR1+ macrophages as a mechanosensitive channel that triggers NGF synthesis via calcium influx and NF-κB nuclear translocation. This macrophage-derived NGF sensitizes TRPV1+ nociceptors, establishing a direct mechanosensory relay independent of cytokine cascades. Genetic ablation of Piezo1, Ngf, or Ntrk1 abolished visceral hyperalgesia in colitis models.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Piezo1 in CX3CR1+ macrophages directly transduces mechanical cues into nociceptive signals during colitis",
    "Piezo1 activation induces NGF synthesis through calcium influx and NF-κB nuclear translocation",
    "Genetic deletion of Piezo1, Ngf, or Ntrk1 abolishes visceral hyperalgesia in colitis models"
  ],
  "study_type": "Intracolonic zymosan model",
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies tissue-resident macrophages as autonomous mechanical sensors that establish a direct, parallel pain transmission pathway to sensory nerves during inflammatory conditions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a plasmonic coacervate platform for detecting polystyrene micro/nanoplastics (MNPs) in water. The platform uses liquid-liquid phase separation to form charged droplets that spontaneously capture PS MNPs with high enrichment rates. It integrates silver nanoparticles to create SERS hotspots, achieving detection limits of 1–10 ng/mL and high recovery rates in environmental samples.",
  "key_findings": [
    "99.4% enrichment rate for nanoscale PS MNPs",
    "91.1% enrichment rate for microscale PS MNPs",
    "SERS enhancement factor of 2.72 × 109 with detection limits of 1–10 ng/mL"
  ],
  "study_type": "Plasmonic coacervate platform",
  "scientific_significance": "This approach provides a sensitive, rapid method for detecting environmental micro/nanoplastics using spontaneous sequestration and plasmonic amplification, advancing strategies for monitoring plastic pollution in water systems."
}
